  "description": "Recruiter-style questions for the AI backend (S09), graded against the real published content in src/content (the same context the Lambda gets). Grading rules: see evals/grade.ts (recall is required everywhere; precision only for detail and multiturn; forbidSources and mustNotMention catch fabrication, not mentions of real related skills; declineMayCite lets a decline still cite facts). mustMention entries are all required; alternatives inside one entry are separated by '|'. Matching ignores case and accents. Expected facts come only from the content files: when content changes, update the affected questions. mustNotMentionAnywhere applies to every answer: the content never gives the author's name, so any name is invented (the model guessed one from link handles).",
